r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12439\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n(This PR will remain a draft while more tests are performed)\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces new methods to `AudioStreamPlaybackPolyphonic` that further improves flexibility, giving users more control of the streams. This allows for better custom audio systems.\r\nIdeally, this should be merged along with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120761\r\n\r\nHack:\r\nThis PR introduces the option to pause streams. Since that's a bit of a more complex operation, what happens internally when the relevant method is called is that the current playback position is recorded, and the stream is stopped. The `Stream` is still active, and its `pause` property is set. When resumed, `start()` is called on the relevant stream playback with the recorded time, and `pause` is cleared.\r\n\r\nCompatibility:\r\nThis PR breaks compatibility, by renaming `is_stream_playing` to `is_id_valid`. The method does the same thing, however, with the possibility of streams being paused, having both `is_stream_paused` and `is_stream_playing` wouldn't make sense. And all that the original method did was checking if a given ID is valid.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/